;; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;; grammar.enta — THE authoritative `.enta` grammar, in one annotated file.
;;
;; ── Where it lives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;; One file per app: `apps/<name>.enta`, beside an optional `apps/<name>.cljs`
;; (a `:source-file` SCI view) exactly as a transform sits beside its code. The
;; importer reads EVERY entity-plane `.ent`/`.entv`/`.enta` from the git tree and
;; deep-merges them STRICTLY (a same-key collision throws — no silent winner).
;; `apps/` is entity plane, so an `apps/*.cljs` edit publishes back THROUGH its
;; `.enta` — the exporter (`emit-app-file`) round-trips the pair byte-stably. That
;; also means the tree is DERIVED: a file the schema no longer produces is dropped
;; from the next projection, and one it still produces is written back however
;; often you delete it locally (see "HOW TO RETIRE ONE" below).
;;
;; ── OBJECT-ORIENTED, not a dashboard of wires ───────────────────────────────
;; Start from the OBJECTS (OOUX, Sophia Prater): a list of them (`:object-table`
;; with `:active`), the selected one's OWN view beside it (`:object-view` — the
;; same page it has everywhere, with its Actions on it), and a page to create
;; one (`:action-form` of a create Action). `template.enta` is exactly that. Hand-
;; wired variables for every number are the exception, not the skeleton.
;; An app is not the only door: a WORKSPACE (`:workspaces` in the `.ent`) can
;; offer an object type directly — `{:kind :object-type :object-type :auftrag}`
;; on its home page opens that type's list and views, no app needed.
;;
;; Writeback is level 2/3 only: a widget merely TRIGGERS it (`:action-button`,
;; `:comments :action`, `:submit`) naming an Action authored in the `.ent`
;; (`:actions`, ~L834; an edit `:functions` entry, ~L918). So `wartungskosten`
;; is not "lossy": its €/Std is a level-1 `:expr` here; only a value the whole
;; ontology reuses drops down to `:derived`.
;;
;;   :live false                        ; aus — die Ansicht zeigt den Stand vom Oeffnen
;;   :live {:types [:anfrage-verlauf]}  ; nur diese, statt aller gebundenen Typen
;;   :live {:min-seconds 10}            ; Boden zwischen zwei Lesezugriffen
;;
;; Was ANKOMMT, entscheidet der Server: kennt der Lauf seine geschriebenen Zeilen
;; (eine Aktion fuehrt sie), schickt er `objectSetChanged` mit den Objekten;
;; sonst `refreshObjectSet` — "reload the object set". Ein Build meldet immer das
;; zweite: seine Zeilen sind ein Dataset, keine Nachricht.
;;
;; Wer das Abo selbst fuehrt (eine eingebettete Ansicht, ein eigener Client),
;; nimmt `app-sdk/watch!` — dieselbe Tuer, die das Portal benutzt.
;;
;; ── The complete widget vocabulary (Dialect B — app_sdk `widget-registry`) ──
;; A leaf is `{:widget <kw> …config}`; every value may be a reactive reference —
;; `{:from <type>}` (payload object set) · `{:var <name>}` (state handle, an
;; interactive `:sel`) · `{:val <name>}` (a variable's value). The KEY set per
;; widget is what the grammar enforces (closed maps; a typo is a load error).
;;
;; Two more single-key maps are TEMPLATE FILLS, not reactive refs — substituted
;; from a CONTEXT rather than resolved from the vars graph (see the containers
;; below): `{:item <prop>}` / `{:item-not <prop>}` inside a `:loop` `:body` (the
;; clicked/iterated object's field, and its boolean negation) · `{:arg <prop>}`
;; inside an `:overlay` `:body` (the payload the overlay was opened with).
;;
;;   RIDERS  (on any node)
;;     :title :hidden? :when                         ; :when a ref/handle → visibility
;;     containers also :bg (:1..:5) :collapse :class
;;     :box {:icon :help :w :min-w :max-w :grow?}     ; per-widget icon/help/sizing
;;     :vars {…}  on any INNER container → a subtree-scoped filter SANDBOX
;;                (layered over the root vars), not just at the root
;;
;;   WAS DIE TUER PRUEFT, bevor ein Push durchgeht (nicht erst zur Laufzeit):
;;     • jede `{:val x}` / `{:var x}` muss eine Variable nennen, die in DIESEM
;;       Bereich deklariert ist — innere `:vars` legen sich ueber aeussere. Ein
;;       Name, der ins Leere zeigt, loeste zu nil auf: das Widget zeigte eine leere
;;       Liste, und die ist von „es gibt wirklich nichts" nicht zu unterscheiden.
;;       AUSNAHME: das `:select` eines Containers — dort duldet die Laufzeit einen
;;       Namen ohne Variable, der Streifen faellt dann auf die erste Lasche zurueck.
;;     • ein Parameter, der eine OBJEKTMENGE verlangt (`:rows`/`:items`/`:shapes`),
;;       darf nicht an eine Variable gebunden sein, die nachweislich einen Skalar
;;       haelt. Wo der Typ sich nicht bestimmen laesst, schweigt die Pruefung —
;;       ein Tor, das gelegentlich irrt, ist schlimmer als keines.
;;     • ein `:type`, der der Form widerspricht, und eine Definitionsart, die der
;;       Typ nicht zulaesst (siehe unten).
;;     • `{:from x}` bedeutet UEBERALL dasselbe: erst die Variable, dann die
;;       Payload. Das war einmal verschieden — im `:vars`-Eintrag beides, auf dem
;;       Blatt nur die Payload — und hat ein Auswahlfeld lange leer stehen lassen.
;;
;; This file is a reference, not an installable app. Config VALUES are illustrative;
;; the KEY set per widget is what the grammar enforces. `bin/sutra` reads live
;; wiring — do not treat this as prod state.
;; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{;; :name — REQUIRED. The app's identity (rename-safe: the file may be named
 ;; anything). Lowered to the `:applications` entry key.
 :name :maengel-konsole

 :display-name "Defects Console"

 ;; :description / :icon — OPTIONAL presentation. An app opens at its published
 ;; version: the first install cuts version 1, :auto-publish true one on every
 ;; save. :project — Pillar-4 ownership (the grant cascade).
 :description "Open defects across the fleet — ground time, load per station, and where they sit."
 :icon        "✈"
 :project     :aviation

 ;; :promoted / :collection — die Portal-Kuration. `:promoted true` stellt die App
 ;; ins App-Portal und VERLANGT eine `:collection` (die Ueberschrift, unter
 ;; der sie dort steht; die Sektion selbst wird in `:collections` des `.ent`
 ;; deklariert, siehe grammar.ent). Ohne `:promoted` ist die App nicht unerreichbar,
 ;; nur unbeworben — sie wird ueber den Workspace geoeffnet, der sie traegt.
 ;; ⚠ Sobald die Instanz ihren ERSTEN Workspace fuehrt, ist der Lint-Riegel
 ;; `:app-outside-every-workspace` scharf: eine `:promoted` App, die auf keinem Regal
 ;; steht, wird abgewiesen — sie waere ein zweiter, unkuratierter Weg hinein.
 :promoted    true
 :collection  :operations

 ;; :tags / :owner / :thumbnail — die Karte im Portal. `:tags` sind die Filter-
 ;; schlagworte, `:owner` der zustaendige Mensch (frei, kein Principal-Verweis),
 ;; `:thumbnail` das Bild auf der Kachel.
 :tags        [:maengel :ops]
 :owner       "Betrieb"
 :thumbnail   "maengel-card.png"

 ;; :repository — nur zu setzen, wenn der besitzende Klon nicht aus dem Pfad folgt.
 ;; Eine `.entv` braucht ihn nie und darf ihn nicht tragen.
 :repository  :aviation-apps

 ;; :object-types — the SETS this app is served (their rows arrive in the payload,
 ;; addressable as {:from <type>}). :aggregate-types — types the app may aggregate
 ;; on the SERVER but is not served row-by-row. :functions — query Functions the app
 ;; may run for a function-backed object set ({:function <name>} var). All folded
 ;; into :layout by enta->schema (the server reads an app's scope from :layout).
 ;;
 ;; ── TESTING a {:function <name>} var (query Function) ───────────────────────
 ;; A query Function is a CODE `:functions` entry in the code repository's `.ent`
 ;; (python: `@function` from `functions.api`, not `@transform`; NO :output — it
 ;; RETURNS rows). Test it in this order:
 ;;   1. it lands — `projection push <text> --preview`, then push and commit;
 ;;      `function show <name>` lists it.
 ;;   2. its rows — `function run <name> k=v …` runs it on the server, read-only.
 ;;      Arguments bind by the ATTRIBUTE name (`flug-id`), and a hidden attribute
 ;;      never reaches it.
 ;;   3. the app — whitelist it under `:functions` and open the app. `app-data`
 ;;      does NOT run functions, so a green `app-data` tests nothing here.
 :object-types    [:mangel :station]
 :aggregate-types [:arbeitsschritt]
 :functions       [:dringlichste-maengel]

 :actions [{:action :station-anlegen}]

 ;; Headless: `bin/enta derived <datei>.enta` lists them, `bin/enta derived-add …`
 ;; is the panel's form on a terminal — same rules, same door.
 :derived-properties
 {:mangel {:arbeitsstunden     {:kind :aggregation :over :mangel-arbeitsschritt :agg :sum
                                 :of :stunden :where [:= :jahr {:val :jahr}]}
           :schritte           {:kind :aggregation :over :mangel-arbeitsschritt :agg :count}
           :stunden-je-schritt {:kind :column-math :label "Stunden je Schritt"
                                 :expression [:div :arbeitsstunden :schritte]}
           ;; the column the :hits table binds as {:prop :liegezeit-minuten}
           :liegezeit-minuten  {:kind :column-math :label "Min"
                                 :expression [:* :liegezeit 60]}}}

 ;; :layout — the Dialect-B node tree (the SHARED grammar). A standalone app's
 ;; root is usually a container over object SETS with a :vars cross-filter graph.
 :layout
 {;; The reactive graph, read at the ROOT. A STATE handle an interactive widget
  ;; writes; a DERIVED object set recomputed from the vars + payload.
  ;; `:filter-pills` ist MEHRFACHAUSWAEHLEND und schreibt eine MENGE — `#{:vie}`,
  ;; und `#{}` fuer „All". Daraus folgen beide Zeilen hier, und beide sind schon
  ;; falsch gebaut worden: `:type :array` (also die EDN-Kodierung), weil
  ;; `:keyword`/`:number`/`:boolean` eine Menge beim Gang durch die URL
  ;; VERSTUEMMELN — `parseInt "#{3}"` ist NaN, und jede nichtleere Menge ist
  ;; truthy, also schreibt `:bool` fuer `#{false}` dasselbe wie fuer `#{true}`.
  ;; Und `:in` statt `:=`, weil `:=` STRIKT ist: eine Zahl ist nie gleich einer
  ;; Menge, und die leere Auswahl muss WEITEN, nicht leeren.
  :vars {:view        {:type :keyword :default :overview
                       :external-id :view :in-url :when-visible}           ; the page shown
         :profile     {:type :keyword :default :planer}               ; the variant shown
         :station-sel {:type :array :default #{}
                       :external-id :station :in-url :when-visible}        ; state handle
         :maengel     {:from :mangel                                 ; filtered set
                       :where [[:station :in {:var :station-sel}]]}
         ;; Geo: [[:lage :within-distance {:center {:val :ort} :distance 300 :unit :km}]]
         ;; or [[[:lat :lon] :within-bounding-box {:top-left [48.5 12] :bottom-right [46 17]}]];
         ;; a center not yet chosen WEITET, wie eine leere :in-Auswahl.
         :total       {:default-agg [:count :id :mangel]}            ; count of :mangel
         :ranked      {:function :dringlichste-maengel :args {:station {:val :station-sel}}}
         :by-station  {:aggregate {:find     :mangel
                                   :aggs     [{:fn :count :name :maengel}]
                                   :group-by [[:link :mangel-station] :status]}}}

  :kind  :pages
  :select {:var :view}
  :header {:title "Defects console"}
  :pages
  [{:id :overview :label "Overview"
    :body {:kind :rows
           :items
           [{:kind :toolbar
             :items [{:widget :kpi :label "Defects" :value {:val :total}
                      :on-click {:do :set :var {:var :station-sel} :to nil}}
                     {:widget :filter-pills :sel {:var :station-sel}
                      :items [{:value :vie :label "VIE"} {:value :szg :label "SZG"}]
                      :all-label "All"}
                     ;; [NEW FORM] the DOWNLOAD counterpart to :media-uploader —
                     ;; POSTs the file-level :export request (its :params may be refs)
                     {:widget :export :label "Export" :params {:station {:val :station-sel}}
                      :filename "maengel"}]}
            ;; a general chart (Plotly), from a payload set; :box adds help + grow
            {:widget :chart :chart-kind :time-series
             :rows {:val :maengel} :x :tag :y :count :group :ata-kapitel
             :box {:help "Reports per day" :grow? true}}
            ;; [NEW FORM] LAYERS — one chart, two shapes, TWO SCALES: the bars
            ;; count defects against the left axis, the line reads average ground
            ;; time in hours against the RIGHT one (:axis :right), and :kind :trend
            ;; fits a straight line through the measure its :y names, on that
            ;; measure's own axis. Without the second axis the hours would be
            ;; drawn flat along a count scale — readable, and wrong.
            {:widget :chart :rows {:val :maengel} :x :tag
             :series [{:name "Defects" :y :count :kind :bar}
                      {:name "Liegezeit ø" :y :liegezeit :kind :line :axis :right}
                      {:name "Trend"   :y :count :kind :trend}]
             :axes {:left  {:title "Defects" :fmt ",.0f"}
                    :right {:title "h" :fmt ",.1f"}}
             :box {:help "Volume vs. ground time" :grow? true}}
            ;; a token-free map: each row carries its OWN :lat/:lon (a transform's
            ;; job, not the view's); :color/:size are per-row props or constants
            {:widget :map :rows {:from :station} :lat :lat :lon :lng
             :label :name :color :load :style :carto-positron :height 340}]}}

   {:id :neu :label "Neu"
    :body {:kind :rows
           :vars {:neuer-name {:default ""} :neuer-ort {:default ""}
                  :anlege-fehler {:default ""}
                  :regionen {:from :station}}
           :items [{:widget :map :rows {:from :station} :lat :lat :lon :lng
                    :pick :point :sel {:var :neuer-ort}
                    :style :carto-positron :height 320}
                   {:kind :toolbar
                    :items [{:widget :text-input :sel {:var :neuer-name}
                             :placeholder "Name der Station"}
                            {:widget :action-button :label "Anlegen"
                             :busy-label "…" :intent :primary
                             :action :station-anlegen
                             :params {:name {:val :neuer-name}
                                      :standort {:val :neuer-ort}}
                             :disabled? {:val :neuer-ort}}]}
                   {:widget :action-form :action :station-anlegen
                    :label "Anlegen" :busy-label "…" :cancel-label "Verwerfen"
                    :defaults {:standort {:val :neuer-ort}}
                    :options {:region {:val :regionen}}
                    :on-done [{:do :set :var {:var :neuer-ort} :to nil}]
                    :on-cancel [{:do :set :var {:var :neuer-ort} :to nil}]
                    :error-var :anlege-fehler}]}}

   {:id :explore :label "Explore"
    ;; a SUBTREE-scoped sandbox: :vars HERE drive only this section's widgets
    :body {:kind :section :title "Filter defects" :vars {:q {:default ""}
                                                         :hits {:from :mangel
                                                                :where [[:mangel-nr :contains {:var :q}]]}}
           :tag {:widget :kpi :display :tag :label "Defects" :value {:val :total}}
           :items [{:widget :filter-sidebar :title "Filters"
                    :fields [{:label "Number" :kind :search :sel {:var :q}}]}
                   {:widget :object-table :rows {:val :hits}
                    :cols [{:label "No."  :prop :mangel-nr}
                           {:label "Aircraft" :prop :kennzeichen}
                           {:label "Ground h" :prop :liegezeit :fmt :menge :align :right}
                           ;; A COMPUTED column is NOT an :expr here — `ColSpec`
                           ;; refuses the key, because a column BINDS a value and
                           ;; does not compute one. It is declared once under
                           ;; :derived-properties (:kind :column-math) and bound
                           ;; like any property, which is also what makes it
                           ;; SORTABLE and FILTERABLE — a per-cell expression is
                           ;; neither.
                           {:label "Min" :prop :liegezeit-minuten :fmt :menge :align :right}
                           ;; [NEW FORM] a value → :badge conditional-format column
                           {:label "State" :prop :status
                            :badge {"aog"     {:tone :warn :text "AOG"}
                                    :default  {:tone :ok :text "flugfähig"}}}]}
                   ;; MASTER/DETAIL — the table writes the row the reader is on
                   ;; into :active (the first row is pre-selected unless
                   ;; :auto-active? false); a :columns container names that same
                   ;; handle as its :detail column, which on a phone becomes a
                   ;; page of its own:
                   ;;   {:kind :columns :detail {:var :auswahl}
                   ;;    :items [{:widget :object-table :rows {:val :hits}
                   ;;             :cols [{:label "No." :prop :mangel-nr}]
                   ;;             :active {:var :auswahl} :auto-active? true}
                   ;;            {:widget :object-view :object {:var :auswahl}}]}
                   {:widget :markdown :text "> Type a defect number to filter."}]}}

   ;; :profiles — the viewer's profile picks ONE variant (no strip).
   ;; :visibility gates this whole tab to a role (empty list would = all).
   {:id :ops :label "By role" :visibility {:roles [:ops :admin]}
    :body {:kind :profiles :select {:var :profile} :default :planer
           :variants [{:id :planer :body {:widget :kpi :label "Open" :value {:val :total}}}
                      ;; The pivot over the SERVER aggregate: :row names the
                      ;; linked-object dimension (its value is the station bucket
                      ;; {:id … :title …} → the pivot labels by :title, groups by
                      ;; :id), :col the scalar status, :value the metric. Each cell
                      ;; is one server bucket, so :sum just surfaces its count.
                      {:id :manager    :body {:widget :pivot-table :rows {:val :by-station}
                                              :row :mangel-station :col :status
                                              :value :maengel :agg :sum}}]}}

   ;; A BOARD page — the loop/events/overlay mechanisms in one place. The :loop
   ;; renders its :body as a TEMPLATE, once per defect ({:item …} fills the card);
   ;; a per-card :button fires a declarative EVENT (a vector: set the selection,
   ;; THEN open the drawer); the :overlay shows the selected defect and clears the
   ;; selection on close. (Three loops over three filtered sets = a Kanban board.)
   {:id :board :label "Board"
    :body {:kind :rows
           :vars {:sel-no {:default nil}
                  :sel    {:from :mangel :where [[:mangel-nr := {:val :sel-no}]]}}
           :items
           [{:kind :loop :items {:val :maengel} :arrange :grid
             :max-columns 3 :min-card-width 240
             ;; [NEW FORM] group the cards by :status — each group subheaded
             :group-by :status :group-label :text
             :empty {:widget :markdown :text "_no defects_"}
             :body {:kind :section :bg :2
                    :body {:kind :rows
                           :items [{:widget :markdown :text {:item :mangel-nr}}
                                   {:widget :badge :tone :info :text {:item :status}}
                                   {:widget :button :label "Details" :intent :none
                                    :on-click [{:do :set :var {:var :sel-no} :to {:item :mangel-nr}}
                                               {:do :open :overlay :mdetail}]}]}}}
            {:kind :overlay :overlay :mdetail :as :drawer :side :right :title "Defect"
             :on-close {:do :set :var {:var :sel-no} :to nil}
             :body {:widget :object-table :rows {:val :sel}
                    :cols [{:label "No."   :prop :mangel-nr}
                           {:label "Ground h" :align :right :prop :liegezeit :fmt :menge}]}}]}}]}}

;; ── An SCI-authored app instead of a data layout — the LEGACY road ──────────
;; An app whose view is hand-written ClojureScript carries NO :layout; it names a
;; sibling `:source-file` (client-inlined to :source on install, exactly as a
;; python transform's :code-file → :code). The rest of the wrapper is identical:
;;   {:name :capacity-planner
;;    :description "…" :icon "📊" :project :aviation
;;    :object-types [:station]
;;    :source-file "apps/capacity_planner.cljs"}
;;
;; Do not start here. The FE routes a data `:layout` AHEAD of `:source`
;; (`apphost/registry.cljs`), so an app that has both renders from the
;; layout and the `.cljs` is dead weight that still ships to every viewer.
;;
;; ── HOW TO RETIRE ONE — deleting the `.cljs` now HOLDS ──────────────────────
;; It did not always. `:source` is omit-preserved like every other field, so a
;; push that merely dropped `:source-file` left the stored view standing, and the
;; exporter wrote `apps/<name>.cljs` back into the tree on the very next schema
;; write. With `SUTRA_APP_SOURCE_OMIT_CLEARS` on (prod, since 2026-08-15), an app
;; declaration that carries a `:layout` and NO `:source` RETRACTS the stored view:
;;   1. author the `:layout` (this file is the vocabulary) and push it — verify
;;      the app renders from data alone;
;;   2. in ONE commit, drop `:source-file` from the `.enta` and `git rm` the
;;      `apps/<name>.cljs`;
;;   3. the install clears `:source`, the exporter stops emitting the sibling, and
;;      `normalized by install` removes it from the tree.
;; Both halves matter: a `.enta` that still names a `:source-file` whose blob is
;; gone is NOT a retraction. And the reset is narrow on purpose — a metadata-only
;; update (no `:layout`, e.g. `repository place`) still preserves the view, so a
;; partial push cannot blank an app by accident.

;; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;; THREE APP CAPABILITIES — authorable from a DATA `.enta` (Upload · Export ·
;; Scenario forks). `:upload`/`:export` are FILE-LEVEL keys that `enta->schema`
;; folds INTO `:layout` (where the server reads `[:layout :upload]`/`[:layout
;; :export]`), the exact pattern as `:object-types`; `emit-app-file` lifts them
;; back out, so the round-trip is byte-stable. The scenario surface is a widget +
;; a layout-root rider. (Grammar: `DataAppFile`/`UploadSpec`/`ExportSpec` +
;; `:scenario-picker`/`::container :scenario` in `parser/ent.clj`.)
;;
;; Sie läuft NACH dem Build: ihre Edits landen auf den Objekten, die der Build
;; gerade materialisiert hat, und bleiben als `object_edits`-Overlay über jeden
;; späteren Rebuild bestehen („user edits win"). Vor dem Build gestartet schriebe
;; sie auf Zeilen, die es noch nicht gibt. Schlägt sie fehl, ist der Upload
;; trotzdem gelandet — das Ergebnis reitet neben ihm in der Antwort unter
;; `:action`, so wie das des Builds unter `:build`.
;;
;; ── (2) :export — the READ-side generator (ODS / ad-hoc python) ─────────────
;; POST /api/my-application/:rid/export → fill a spreadsheet template from the
;; app's bound objects for a chosen period, hand back the `.ods` (base64) to
;; download. `server.clj my-application-export`: sums `:value-field` per
;; `:key-field` over objects matching the period, runs `:code` in the NETLESS
;; python jail. `:cumulative-field` (e.g. :monat) matches as `≤` → year-to-date.
;; Author the template + generator as sibling FILES; the CLI inlines
;; `:template-file`→`:template-b64` and `:code-file`→`:code` on install, and the
;; exporter externalises them back to `exports/<app>.<ext>` (round-trip verified).
;; Used by kostenverlauf.
;;   :export {:object-type      :kostenzeile
;;            :key-field        :konto :value-field :betrag
;;            :period-fields    [:jahr :monat]     ; whitelisted request params
;;            :cumulative-field :monat             ; matched ≤ (YTD); omit = equality
;;            :template-file    "exports/kostenverlauf.ods"  ; CLI → :template-b64
;;            :code-file        "exports/kostenverlauf.py"   ; CLI → :code
;;            :python-deps      ["odfpy"] :filename "kostenverlauf" :profile :default}
;;
;;   THE SCENARIO HANDLE MAY BE IN THE URL — and should be, so the selected fork
;;   survives a reload, moves with Back/Forward and travels in a shared link. It
;;   needs an `:external-id` to say so: that id is the query parameter's key, and
;;   `:in-url` says whether the app writes it back. That
;;   was BROKEN until 2026-08-20: the SDK `add-watch`es the active-scenario handle
;;   to re-read the payload on a switch, an addressed var is a `ViewCursor`, and the
;;   cursor implemented only IDeref/IReset/ISwap — so `add-watch` threw
;;   "No protocol method IWatchable.-add-watch" from inside a component
;;   constructor and the WHOLE app painted as the error box. The cursor is
;;   watchable now (`view-state`), delegating to the URL store and filtered to its
;;   own param.
;;
;;      (a) the ARRAY comes from a multi picker:
;;            :vars {:szen {:type :array :default []
;;                          :external-id :szen :in-url :always}}
;;            {:widget :scenario-picker :sel {:var :szen} :multi? true}
;;          `:multi? true` writes a VECTOR of segs (a checkbox strip); without it
;;          the picker writes one seg, which is what a `:scenario` rider wants.
;;
;;      (b) a `:compare` VAR reads one object set on the base AND each fork:
;;            :koepfe {:source :mitarbeiter :where [[:aktiv := 1]]}
;;            :vergl  {:compare {:of :koepfe :scenarios {:var :szen}
;;                               :key :mitarbeiter-nr}}
;;          `:of` must name a DERIVED var (`:source`/`:from`): the spec is
;;          RE-RESOLVED against each branch's payload, and that is the whole trick
;;          — a comparison needs no second layout and no server-side diff. An
;;          `:aggregate`/`:function` var is refused (its handle already belongs to
;;          one branch, and comparing a branch with itself is worse than an error).
;;          `:key` is the BUSINESS key rows are matched on, not the object id: a
;;          fork can carry an object the base never had, and an id-join would show
;;          it as a row from nowhere. Each fork costs one payload read, cached.
;;
